// The RSASSA-PKCS1-v1_5 signing negative-composition probe world: the
// minimal consumer of `rsassa-pkcs1-v15-sign`, which the in-guest provider
// deliberately does not export (class D — see
// rust/guest-provider/README.md). The class-D gate
// (`just conformance::class-d`) builds a dummy component of this world and
// asserts it does NOT compose with the provider.
//
// The signing guest cannot prove this: its composition already fails on
// `ecdsa-sign`. This world imports nothing the provider withholds except
// `rsassa-pkcs1-v15-sign` itself, so its composition failure can only come
// from that interface — the provider's `signature` export rebinds the key
// resources and orphans the import (the mechanism is documented on
// `../oaep-probe/wit/world.wit` and in the `class-d` recipe).
//
// The `lann:webcrypto` package lives once at the repository root `wit/`,
// pulled in through the `deps/lann-webcrypto` symlink.
package conformance:class-d-rsassa-sign-probe;

world rsassa-sign-probe {
    @unstable(feature = rsa-sign)
    import lann:webcrypto/rsassa-pkcs1-v15-sign@0.1.0;
}
